## OV02C10 addition in the jc8012_camera plugin

The files `ov02c10_sensor.c`, `ov02c10.h`, `ov02c10_compat.h`,
`ov02c10_regs.h`, `ov02c10_settings.h`, and `ov02c10_types.h` were copied
from https://github.com/sullb/esphome-p4-csi-camera (MIT License) on 2026-10-18.
That project identifies the register tables as based on the Linux OV02C10
driver; the driver structure follows Espressif's esp_cam_sensor drivers
(Apache-2.0, see the SPDX headers). The complete plugin is distributed under
GPL-3.0-only; upstream copyright and license notices remain applicable to these
files.

As required by GPLv3 §5(a): `ov02c10_sensor.c` was modified on 2026-10-19
(exposure, gain and orientation on the OV02C10's own registers, as the Linux
driver drivers/media/i2c/ov02c10.c sets them; OV5640 registers removed; the chip
id is checked). Its header comment lists the changes. `esp_video_camera.cpp`
calls `ov02c10_sensor_link_anchor()` and `__init__.py` adds the files below.

`build_stubs/ov02c10_ipa/ov02c10.json` is an IPA (image tuning) configuration
derived from Espressif's `sc2336_default_p4_eco4.json` (esp_cam_sensor,
Apache-2.0) on 2026-10-19: the same blocks under the name OV02C10, with a wider
white balance search range and a neutral saturation. Since 0.2.3 it also has
the black level and the brightness-dependent gamma of Espressif's rev3
tunings (`sc2336_default_p4_eco5.json`, `os02n10_default_p4_eco5.json`), and
its colour matrix is halfway between the SC2336 one and neutral. Since 0.2.4 its
white balance scales red and blue (1.15, 1.3), as the rev3 SC2336 tuning does
(1.1, 1.1).

Since 0.2.5 `__init__.py` takes `jpeg_quality` as esp_video does (1 to 100,
higher is better, default 80) instead of 1 to 63 (default 10); the default in
`esp_video_camera.h` follows. The `CMakeLists.txt` and
`project_include.cmake` beside it are this plugin's own.

The earlier `cfg/sc202cs.json` was removed: no sensor of this board uses it.

Local change: esp_video is taken from the Espressif git master (commit 3bb32ee9ee42b35cfbfeb64ecbc38a7a2222dd71, path esp_video),
which contains the CSI fix for ESP32-P4 silicon revisions < 3.
